1. Qualcomm QAIRT / QNN
----------------------

On-device compilation uses qnn-context-binary-generator and Qualcomm libraries,
including libQnnHtp, libQnnHtpPrepare, libQnnSystem, HTP skeleton/stub libraries
and backend extensions. These files are not distributed in this repository.
Developers supply an appropriately licensed SDK; placement is documented in
docs/BUILD.md.

Permission to redistribute a complete APK containing these files has not been
established by this project. The source license does not authorize their
redistribution. Packaging and distribution rights are a topic for review with
Qualcomm.

2. Checked-in UNet template provenance
-------------------------------------

The original SD1.5 recipe and trimmed pack were derived from a UNet exported
using modified diffusers code distributed through xororz's Local Dream under
CC BY-NC 4.0, then processed with QAIRT. The original diffusers project is
Apache-2.0; that does not remove the separate provenance of the modified exporter
used for these artifacts.

The checked-in template bundle is treated as non-commercial and excluded from
the repository's MIT grant. Commercial use requires independently establishing
the necessary rights or regenerating appropriate artifacts from an independently
licensed export path. See template/README.md and docs/TEMPLATE-AUTHORING.md.
The conversion engine accepts separately authored templates.

3. Generated model libraries and component assets
------------------------------------------------

Pack-loading libqnn_model.so libraries are built from QAIRT-generated model code.
They remain excluded from source control. SDXL templates and the generated
components_sd15/components_sdxl directories are also excluded. Their absence
means a fresh source clone is not sufficient to build a working converter APK.

CLIP recipes reconstruct the checkpoint's MNN-format text encoders and embeddings;
VAE recipes populate QNN encoder and decoder graphs from that checkpoint's
weights. Generated recipes remove learned reference payloads. Their format and
authoring process are documented in docs/CLIP-COMPONENTS.md and
docs/VAE-TEMPLATES.md. Template preparation does not change any applicable
upstream terms.

4. Checkpoints, adapters and shared components
---------------------------------------------

Users supply checkpoints and LoRAs under their respective licenses. New SD1.5
and SDXL conversions use the selected checkpoint's own CLIP and VAE weights.
The standard tokenizer is bundled in locally prepared assets.

The legacy backup workflow can download shared-component archives from xororz's
Local Dream collections and the maintainer's SDXL-OnDevice-Conversion collection.
Those archives are not inputs to new checkpoint conversions. They retain their
original terms, including model and QAIRT artifact restrictions. The historical
SDXL shared VAE was derived from madebyollin/sdxl-vae-fp16-fix.

The debug DSP probe may use a separately supplied libstable_diffusion_core.so
built from CC BY-NC 4.0 upstream code. That binary is excluded and is not part of
the MIT source distribution.

